
The KPI catalogue defines the approved business meaning, calculation basis, and reporting purpose of each metric. Before a KPI is published, confirm its source columns, implement the base measure in DAX, test filter behavior, reconcile the result with Snowflake, and document the approved definition. Use the same validated measure across report pages to maintain consistency.

For semi-additive metrics such as outstanding exposure, explicitly document the reporting-date logic—for example, latest available balance, month-end balance, or balance as of a selected date—so users can interpret results correctly.

